Source: postgresql-oauth-validator
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Roman Pertl <roman@pertl.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-server-dev-all (>= 18), libkrb5-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/roock/postgresql-oauth_validator
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/roock/postgresql-oauth_validator
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/roock/postgresql-oauth_validator.git

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-oauth-validator
Architecture: any
Depends: postgresql-PGVERSION, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, 
Description: OAuth 2.0 token validator for PostgreSQL
 This module implements a simple OAuth 2.0 token validator for built-in
 support of the Device Authorization Flow. The validator performs minimal
 validation by extracting the 'sub' (subject) and 'scope' fields from the
 JWT payload, comparing the token's scopes with those required by the
 pg_hba.conf entry, and mapping the authentication identity 'sub' to a
 database role using pg_ident.conf.
